    "title": "Prime Video's 'Cross' renewed for Season 3 - UPI.com",
    "text": "Trending Supersonic jet Strait of Hormuz 'Vaping' squirrels Coco Gauff Cheesesteaks record Russian tanker Lottery win 'Harry Potter' Meteorite hunters TV March 18, 2026 / 3:17 PM Prime Video's 'Cross' renewed for Season 3 By Fred Topel 1 of 5 | Aldis Hodge, seen at the 2025 Critics Choice Awards in Santa Monica, Calif., will return in Season 3 of \"Cross.\" File Photo by Jim Ruymen/UPI.. | License Photo March 18 (UPI) -- Prime Video announced Wednesday that it has renewed Cross for a third season. The Season 2 finale premiered today. Aldis Hodge plays James Patterson's detective, Alex Cross. Ben Watkins created the show, with new mysteries not based on the books. Watkins did incorporate other characters, like Cross's best friend, John Sampson, played by Isaiah Mustafa. FBI agent Kyle Craig became Kayla Craig, played by Alona Tal. Cross premiered in 2024. Samantha Walkes, Juanita Jennings, Caleb Elijah, Melody Hurd and Johnny Ray Gill also star. Morgan Freeman portrayed detective Alex Cross in two movies based on the novels Kiss the Girls and Along Came a Spider. Tyler Perry played him in 2012's Alex Cross based on Patterson's Cross. Prime Video did not specify when Season 3 will go into production or air. Read More Aldis Hodge: 'Cross' brings beloved literary detective into 2024 'Scarpetta' returning for Season 2 on Prime Video John Krasinski returns as Jack Ryan in new Prime Video movie Topics James PattersonJohn SampsonMorgan FreemanTyler Perry Around the Web Latest Headlines TV // 45 minutes ago '90 Day Fiance' to return May 10 with new cast March 26 (UPI) -- TLC series \"90 Day Fiancé\" returns May 10 with a new cast of international couples. The show follows Americans and their international partners. TV // 3 hours ago Bill Maher to receive the Kennedy Center's Mark Twain Prize March 26 (UPI) -- Stand-up comedian and Real Time host Bill Maher is to receive the Kennedy Center's Mark Twain Prize for American Humor on June 28 in Washington, D.C. TV // 3 hours ago Kim Raver, Kevin McKidd announce they're leaving 'Grey's Anatomy' March 26 (UPI) -- \"Grey's Anatomy\" cast members Kim Raver and Kevin McKidd have announced they are leaving the ABC medical drama. Their final episode is May 7. TV // 4 hours ago Dawnn Lewis, Glynn Turman to star in 'A Different World' sequel series March 26 (UPI) -- \"A Different World\" veterans Dawnn Lewis and Glynn Turman have joined the ensemble of the classic sitcom's sequel. TV // 5 hours ago HBO Max releases first teaser for 'Harry Potter' series March 26 (UPI) -- HBO Max has released its first teaser for the upcoming \"Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone\" series. Nick Frost and John Lithgow co-star. TV // 6 hours ago Pangolin eliminated in 'Masked Singer' semi-finals March 26 (UPI) -- A celebrity dressed as a pangolin was eliminated from \"The Masked Singer\" Season 14 semi-finals in Los Angeles Wednesday night. Nick Cannon hosts. TV // 1 day ago 'Squid Game' star Lee Byung-hun, Han Ji-min to star in 'The Koreans' March 25 (UPI) -- Disney+ has started filming \"The Koreans,\" a new drama inspired by the FX series \"The Americans,\" which starred Keri Russell and Matthew Rhys. TV // 1 day ago TV review: 'Daredevil: Born Again' Season 2 slows down revival LOS ANGELES, March 24 (UPI) -- After a rousing first season, \"Daredevil: Born Again,\" premiering Tuesday on Disney+, resumes more normal television plot. mechanics to its detriment. TV // 1 day ago Peyton List's 'School Spirits' renewed for Season 4 March 24 (UPI) -- Paramount+ has renewed its supernatural drama, \"School Spirits,\" for a fourth season. Peyton List, Kristian Ventura and Milo Manheim co-star. TV // 2 days ago 'Criminal Minds' Season 19 to premiere on Paramount+ May 28 March 24 (UPI) -- Paramount+ has announced Season 19 of \"Criminal Minds: Evolution\" is set to premiere on May 28. Connor Storrie from \"Heated Rivalry\" guest stars. Trending Stories WWE: Sid to be inducted into Hall of Fame class of 2026 Stephen Colbert announced to write 'Lord of the Rings' movie Famous birthdays for March 26: Michael Imperioli, Ella Anderson Chip Taylor, singer-songwriter who wrote 'Wild Thing,' dies at 86 Kim Raver, Kevin McKidd announce they're leaving 'Grey's Anatomy' Follow Us CLOSE X Why are you reporting this ad? Please make a selection. Plays sound Contains adult content Covers the page Other Additional Information Please help us by describing the ad. Only 500 characters are allowed. Report ad Thank you for letting us know. This ad has already been reported. Powered by ×",
